this event is put on by the vegas  chamber the theme this year is battle  reborn as the las vegas economy comes  back from the pandemic at the vegas  chambers preview las vegas event  governor steve sisilak said about 11 000  new jobs are coming in the next few  years in manufacturing ev companies and  distribution facilities some new things  coming into the state coming into  southern nevada despite the omicron wave  the governor projects southern nevada's  economic future will be a bright one i  don't plan on having to take any steps  backwards we're moving forward in the  fight against covet and omicron right  now and we're going to continue to move  forward we're working on economic  diversification in bringing new and  emerging industries here to southern  nevada the las vegas economy will also  benefit from hosting major events like  the nfl draft and the super bowl prices  are not expected to drop anytime soon  though inflation is a big challenge for  our small businesses especially as the  price of goods increases and then  another thing that our small businesses  are having trouble with is the talent  pool these are all challenges that we at  the vegas chamber are working to help  them overcome the vegas chambers said it  was a pretty big deal for them to be  able to host this event inside a legion  stadium the governor noted it's a place  that opened during the darkest days of  the pandemic hector mejia reporting live  local now
 

